# Desktop code simplification

Branch: `code-simplification`, from committed and pushed checkpoint
`94aeeee149b75b4c851931e1138e5bedfcac5aff` (`host-cleanup`). The operator authorized
completion of all five items below without intermediate approval stops. No merge,
release or deployment is implied. Preserve the earlier candidate packages.

## Required work

1. Delete unsupported Windows Host scaffolding, dependencies and dormant settings,
   plus verified unused Client helpers. Keep active Linux CUDA/DRM/X11, native
   macOS code, license attribution and Git history.
2. Establish one encoding-profile catalog for stable IDs, wire names, precision,
   capture compatibility and dimension restrictions. Consume it in the desktop
   Client and both Hosts; preserve independent runtime hardware qualification.
3. Give complete encoded Client frames one owned backing buffer. Preserve bounded
   queues, keyframe/gap recovery, NAL validation, SPS corrections, timestamps and
   shutdown ownership. Remove redundant NAL-payload/reassembly copies; measure
   allocation/copy changes without claiming unmeasured live latency gains.
4. Consolidate connection/recovery transitions under the existing Client session
   worker. Keep durable cancellation and GUI responsiveness; preserve takeover,
   authentication failure, renderer retention and held-input release behavior.
5. Move macOS display/takeover operations outside the shared runtime lock using
   explicit reservation and completion validation. Preserve graphical ownership,
   authorization, generation checks, restoration and asynchronous shutdown.

## Completion checks

Each item needs production integration and focused behavioral regressions, not
just new abstractions or source assertions. Exercise malformed profile/frame
input, queue overflow and retirement, reconnect/cancel/stop ordering, and Mac
display/takeover races. Keep protocol IDs and wire schemas stable unless an
actual incompatible change requires explicit negotiation.

Run all four hosted candidate builds, signing/notarizing the Mac packages through
the protected workflow. Collect package manifests and hashes. Update HANDOFF
with exact source pins, test results and remaining installed acceptance. Hardware
GPU/color, audio soak, Wacom, login/logout and real display restoration cannot be
claimed from hosted compilation or fixtures alone.

## Status

All five production changes, focused regressions, hosted builds and package
collection are complete for candidate `1.3.05-code-simplification`. Root and
nested changes are committed and pushed on `code-simplification`; no merge,
release or installation was performed.

Encoded frames have one reference-counted allocation containing the queue entry,
NAL views and padded payload. FFmpeg retains the same allocation for ordinary
frames; SPS rewriting and noncontiguous parameter sets retain an explicit copy
path. The transport-to-C boundary still copies once. The fixture measures one
allocation and no NAL/reassembly copies for a four-MiB delta frame; it does not
measure end-to-end latency.

The existing Client worker owns successful startup/recovery transitions;
callbacks can request recovery or durable cancellation. A single lifecycle state
replaces overlapping flags, and late GUI completions cannot reopen input after
stopping. No additional worker is introduced.

Mac display preparation, takeover drain and restoration reserve an operation
under the runtime lock, perform provider work outside it, and revalidate request
authorization and graphical scope before accepting a result. Launch rejects an
outstanding operation or failed restoration. Shutdown cancels preparation and
waits asynchronously for restoration. Synthetic runtime tests exercise the
actual admission lock during provider calls and cancellation during preparation.

Local checks pass: catalog C/C++ contracts, 1,000 lifecycle races, 2,039 encoded
frame/recovery checks and common-C input/queue regressions. Hosted Ubuntu
ASan/UBSan component checks and Mac runtime transaction regressions pass.
Linux Host input lifecycle and three 150-Mbit/s loss-matrix trials pass.
Both signed/notarized Mac packages, the Linux Host RPM and Ubuntu Client DEB
are collected and checksum-verified under
`artifacts/packages/candidates/1.3.05-code-simplification/`.

Builds: Linux Host `41378937781`, Ubuntu Client `41379496268`, Mac Host
`41378048318`, Mac Client `41378323417`. Exact snapshots, original manifests,
logs and local reports are retained in
`artifacts/qualification/code-simplification-1.3.05/`; HANDOFF records the
implementation pins. Installed hardware/session acceptance remains pending.


## Follow-up simplification pass

Authorized in full after the 1.3.05 checkpoint at root `0a32513`. Complete all
items on this branch, then build matching hosted candidates; no merge/release.

- Remove the retired two-connection transport, preserving native configuration,
  authentication, cancellation, FEC and current wire/ABI values.
- Make Client decoding follow FFmpeg send/drain semantics with interruptible
  input waits, packet retry and explicit metadata retirement on errors.
- Assemble Host video metadata and encoded bytes once before queue submission.
- Bound native video queues by bytes and count with accounted overflow.
- Compile focused Host input/crypto tests; replace brittle source assertions
  where behavioral coverage exists; remove duplicate Qt build declarations.
- Delete unreachable Client AV1, Linux Host Apple startup and unused KMS helper.
- Replace per-bookmark polling sleeps with a cancellation-aware timed wait.
- Remove unused wide-character logging and deprecated codecvt setup after
  verifying UTF-8 logging behavior.

Preserve live login-screen audio, 10-bit SDR/identity color paths, exact-format
hardware qualification, input recovery and package ownership/security gates.

All eight implementations are committed and pushed. The four 1.3.06 hosted
builds passed and their packages were collected. Both Mac packages are signed
and notarized. A final Mac-only sender-feature warning cleanup removes an
unused receive timestamp; its signed/notarized 1.3.07 Host rebuild also passed
and is collected. Other products do
not compile that field and retain the validated 1.3.06 packages. No artifact is
relabeled or overwritten.

New production-path checks passed: H.264/HEVC send/drain decoding, bounded
packet retry, polling stop/wait races, variable-size queue eviction accounting,
one-allocation video-record ownership and actual UTF-8 Host logging under the
C locale. Ubuntu ASan/UBSan, compositor, launcher and packaging gates passed.
Host component fixtures passed 25 shuffled repetitions; three 900-frame,
150-Mbit/s 0–5% loss matrices had zero unrecovered frames. Current pins, build
IDs, package locations and remaining installed gates are in HANDOFF.
